  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "VOID Engine 2.2.1\n\n    Hashing\n    - Added Cache32IgnoreCase() and Cache64IgnoreCase() for case-insensitive FNV-1a hashing.\n    - Added separate thread-safe caches with deterministic results regardless of capitalization.\n    - Preserved existing case-sensitive hashing methods.\n\n    Asset Management\n    - Fixed asset cache lookups to ignore filename capitalization.\n    - Prevented duplicate asset loads caused by differently capitalized paths.\n    - Preserved first-load-wins behavior and existing asset settings.\n\n    Input Actions\n    - Made action registration, lookup, removal, and state queries case-insensitive.\n    - Updated string and enum-based action handling.\n    - Preserved existing input snapshots and transition behavior.\n\n    Audio\n    - Fixed SoundInstancePool background worker tracking using Unwrap().\n    - Added safe audio shutdown that cancels and waits for the worker before releasing resources.\n    - Prevented sound instances from being disposed while the background worker is still running.\n\n    Rendering\n    - Added automatic cleanup of pooled render targets during game shutdown.\n    - Dispose VOID-owned render targets while their graphics device is active.\n    - Clear pool references without taking ownership of custom render targets.\n    - Preserved existing render-target pooling and reuse during gameplay.\n\n    Engine Lifecycle\n    - Integrated sound pool shutdown into Game.Dispose() before asset cleanup.\n    - Integrated render-target pool cleanup before window and renderer destruction.\n    - Preserved existing game-loop behavior and window-close safeguards.",
